WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.790 --> 00:00:08.790
- [Donald] I just wanna find 11,780 votes.

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:13.059
- Well, it took some time,

00:00:13.059 --> 00:00:16.730
but it looks like we finally
found some voter fraud.

00:00:16.730 --> 00:00:19.180
We're only a couple of days into 2021

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:22.110
and there is already a new Trump tape.

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:25.630
- [Donald] I have to find 12,000 votes

00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:30.630
and I have them times a lot,
and therefore I won the state.

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:32.670
- It's been just about a
year since President Trump

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:35.070
made the perfect phone call to Ukraine,

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:37.620
where he attempted to
leverage over $400 million

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:40.360
in American taxpayer aid to Ukraine.

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:42.990
- That call was perfect. It
couldn't have been nicer.

00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:44.050
- In an attempt to get help

00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:46.490
against his main political
rival, Joe Biden,

00:00:46.490 --> 00:00:47.810
but it appears that President Trump

00:00:47.810 --> 00:00:50.960
is not done with the 2020 election.

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:54.190
Now, The Washington Post
has obtained bombshell audio

00:00:54.190 --> 00:00:56.330
of over one-hour-long phone call

00:00:56.330 --> 00:00:58.130
between on the one hand, President Trump,

00:00:58.130 --> 00:00:59.650
Mark Meadows and a
lawyer for the president,

00:00:59.650 --> 00:01:01.540
Cleta Mitchell of the
firm Foley &amp; Lardner,

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:02.400
and on the other hand,

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:04.610
Georgia's Secretary of
State, Brad Raffensperger,

00:01:04.610 --> 00:01:07.550
and Secretary of State
General Counsel, Ryan Germany.

00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:09.710
And the parties, for over an hour,

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:11.770
discussed the Georgia election.

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:14.400
And during this call,
President Trump, shall we say,

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:18.370
expresses his extreme concern
about the numbers in Georgia

00:01:18.370 --> 00:01:21.230
that the certified
election results have gone

00:01:21.230 --> 00:01:23.360
for Joe Biden, the president elect.

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:25.610
And on the other hand,
Georgia's Secretary of State,

00:01:25.610 --> 00:01:28.180
Brad Raffensperger, says
that the numbers are correct,

00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:29.370
that there was no impropriety

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:31.350
and that they are very
confident in those numbers

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:32.550
and that the information

00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:35.530
the president has is at best incorrect.

00:01:35.530 --> 00:01:36.900
But our question for today

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:38.880
is whether the newest leaked audio

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:42.420
has put President Trump in
criminal jeopardy or not.

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:44.720
Now, I'm not going to go
into whether you can indict

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:46.180
a sitting president, because
we've talked about that

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:47.790
a million times on this channel.

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:48.660
And also President Trump

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:51.360
is not going to be the sitting
president for very long.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:52.630
Also, let's not get bogged down

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:54.423
in whether he can pardon himself.

00:01:55.270 --> 00:01:56.103
Moving on.

00:01:56.103 --> 00:01:57.480
And not surprisingly,

00:01:57.480 --> 00:02:00.010
already a number of
right-wing outlets are saying

00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:02.440
that the crime is not
the phone call itself,

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:04.240
but the fact that someone would dare

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:06.970
to leak a non-private phone call

00:02:06.970 --> 00:02:09.840
with the president of the United States.

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:11.370
Though I think those arguments,

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:12.800
not only are they made in bad faith,

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:14.770
but here they don't hold water

00:02:14.770 --> 00:02:17.450
because on the morning
that the tape was released,

00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:18.677
President Trump tweeted out,

00:02:18.677 --> 00:02:21.200
"I spoke to Secretary of State
Brad Raffensperger yesterday

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:23.260
about Fulton County and
voter fraud in Georgia.

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:25.550
He was unwilling or
unable to answer questions

00:02:25.550 --> 00:02:27.810
such as the ballots under the table scam,

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:29.900
ballot destruction, out-of-state voters,

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:30.820
dead voters, and more.

00:02:30.820 --> 00:02:32.230
He has no clue!"

00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:34.140
To which Raffensperger responded.

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:35.110
- There was no agreement,

00:02:35.110 --> 00:02:37.750
and we didn't know what the
purpose of the call really was.

00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:39.800
I assumed it was about
the November election,

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:40.660
really, Wednesday.

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:42.640
If President Trump wouldn't
have tweeted out anything

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:43.960
and would have stayed silent,

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:45.770
we would have stayed silent as well.

00:02:45.770 --> 00:02:48.530
- And some people are claiming
that this is a confidential

00:02:48.530 --> 00:02:50.480
settlement conference
regarding litigation.

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:51.580
And while there is such a thing

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:53.430
as confidential settlement agreements,

00:02:53.430 --> 00:02:55.410
I've participated in many of them,

00:02:55.410 --> 00:03:00.410
the thing is if you disclose
the content of that conference,

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:02.320
then arguably you have waived

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:04.910
your privilege to that content.

00:03:04.910 --> 00:03:07.270
So it's likely that even
if privilege attached,

00:03:07.270 --> 00:03:09.470
which I don't think would be the case

00:03:09.470 --> 00:03:11.770
in this particular phone call,

00:03:11.770 --> 00:03:13.130
arguably the president has waived

00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:15.100
any claims of privilege here.

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:18.550
So what's the big deal
about this phone call?

00:03:18.550 --> 00:03:20.260
- [Donald] The people
in the country are angry

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:22.143
and there's nothing wrong with saying

00:03:24.550 --> 00:03:26.070
that you've recalculated.

00:03:26.070 --> 00:03:28.230
- Well, actually there
could be a lot wrong

00:03:28.230 --> 00:03:29.600
with saying that you recalculated

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:32.090
if you haven't actually recalculated,

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:33.920
if you're not allowed to recalculate,

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:36.210
if you recalculate for
pre-textual reasons,

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:38.370
or if you use the recalculation

00:03:38.370 --> 00:03:41.090
to change the numbers inappropriately.

00:03:41.090 --> 00:03:43.350
There's a lot that can be an issue here.

00:03:43.350 --> 00:03:46.110
So let's start with Georgia state law.

00:03:46.110 --> 00:03:49.810
The first part of Georgia
Code Section 21-2-562

00:03:49.810 --> 00:03:51.340
deals with fraudulent entries,

00:03:51.340 --> 00:03:53.380
unlawful alteration or
destruction of entries,

00:03:53.380 --> 00:03:54.820
unlawful removal of documents

00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:57.190
and neglect or refusal
to deliver documents.

00:03:57.190 --> 00:03:59.570
It's obviously against Georgia law

00:03:59.570 --> 00:04:01.940
to falsify documents or
records in connection

00:04:01.940 --> 00:04:05.250
with an election or to
make any false entries.

00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:09.570
And then there's Georgia
Code Section 21-2-576,

00:04:09.570 --> 00:04:12.240
destroying or defacing or
delaying delivery of ballots.

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:13.770
Any person who willfully destroys

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:16.020
or defaces any ballot or
willfully delays the delivery

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:18.440
of any ballots shall be
guilty of a misdemeanor.

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:21.400
Then there's Section 45-11-1,

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:23.050
offenses involving public records,

00:04:23.050 --> 00:04:24.520
documents, or other items.

00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:26.720
It's against Georgia
law for public officials

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:30.150
to falsify any record
related to their office.

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:33.080
And then there's Section 21-2-597,

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:34.720
intentional interference with performance

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:35.940
of election duties.

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:36.773
Under Georgia law,

00:04:36.773 --> 00:04:38.460
any person who intentionally
interferes with,

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:40.880
hinders or delays or
attempts to interfere with,

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:42.110
hinder or delay any other person

00:04:42.110 --> 00:04:44.710
in the performance of any
act or duty authorized

00:04:44.710 --> 00:04:47.670
or imposed by this chapter shall
be guilty of a misdemeanor.

00:04:47.670 --> 00:04:49.890
And that refers to the election duties

00:04:49.890 --> 00:04:52.780
of election-related officials in Georgia.

00:04:52.780 --> 00:04:55.680
And then there's Section 21-2-604,

00:04:55.680 --> 00:04:57.640
good old fashioned criminal solicitation

00:04:57.640 --> 00:04:59.370
to commit election fraud.

00:04:59.370 --> 00:05:00.520
And the important thing to note

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:02.290
in terms of this solicitation defense

00:05:02.290 --> 00:05:05.250
which is actually the case
with most solicitation crimes,

00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:07.010
is that it's not a defense that the person

00:05:07.010 --> 00:05:09.360
you solicited did not take the bait.

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:10.820
And those are just the obvious

00:05:10.820 --> 00:05:12.610
Georgia state-related election crimes.

00:05:12.610 --> 00:05:13.810
Then there's a whole swath

00:05:13.810 --> 00:05:16.000
of federal law related to elections.

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:18.440
The Department of Justice
guidance on federal prosecutions

00:05:18.440 --> 00:05:20.350
for voter fraud states that the following

00:05:20.350 --> 00:05:21.870
are prosecutable election crimes.

00:05:21.870 --> 00:05:23.940
Quote, malfeasance by election officials

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:25.250
acting under color of law,

00:05:25.250 --> 00:05:27.470
such as diluting valid
ballots with invalid ones,

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:29.140
so-called ballot box stuffing,

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:30.780
rendering false vote tabulations,

00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:33.570
or preventing valid voter
registrations or votes

00:05:33.570 --> 00:05:35.700
from being given effect in any election,

00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:38.100
as well as in elections
where federal candidates

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:39.560
are on the ballot.

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:43.340
Now, 18 U.S.C. Sections 241 and 242,

00:05:43.340 --> 00:05:45.560
are the civil rights conspiracy statutes.

00:05:45.560 --> 00:05:47.060
Section 241 states,

00:05:47.060 --> 00:05:49.120
if two or more persons conspire to injure,

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:51.720
oppress, threaten or intimidate
any person in any state

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:53.750
in the free exercise or
enjoyment of any right

00:05:53.750 --> 00:05:55.920
or privilege secured to
him by the Constitution

00:05:55.920 --> 00:05:58.520
or laws of the United States
or because of his having

00:05:58.520 --> 00:06:01.460
so exercised the same, they
shall be fined under this title

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:04.200
or imprisoned not more
than 10 years, or both.

00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:05.810
And the next section, 242,

00:06:05.810 --> 00:06:07.460
makes it a crime for any person acting

00:06:07.460 --> 00:06:09.700
under color of law, statute
ordinance regulation

00:06:09.700 --> 00:06:12.760
or custom to willfully deprive
or cause to be deprived

00:06:12.760 --> 00:06:13.890
from any person those rights,

00:06:13.890 --> 00:06:16.170
privileges or immunities
secured or protected

00:06:16.170 --> 00:06:18.360
by the Constitution and the
laws of the United States.

00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:19.620
That includes depriving people

00:06:19.620 --> 00:06:22.910
of their right to vote and have
their vote properly counted.

00:06:22.910 --> 00:06:25.100
And then the other most
likely applicable federal law

00:06:25.100 --> 00:06:27.610
would be the National
Voter Registration Act,

00:06:27.610 --> 00:06:30.900
now codified as 52 U.S.C. 2501,

00:06:30.900 --> 00:06:32.220
which also makes it illegal

00:06:32.220 --> 00:06:34.490
for election officials to commit fraud,

00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:36.670
specifically anyone who knowingly

00:06:36.670 --> 00:06:38.090
and willfully deprives,

00:06:38.090 --> 00:06:40.110
defrauds or attempts to deprive or defraud

00:06:40.110 --> 00:06:41.270
the residents of a state

00:06:41.270 --> 00:06:44.040
of a fair and impartially
conducted election process

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:47.330
by the procurement, casting
or tabulation of ballots

00:06:47.330 --> 00:06:50.050
that are known by the person
to be materially false,

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:52.210
fictitious or fraudulent under the laws

00:06:52.210 --> 00:06:54.950
of the state in which
the election is held.

00:06:54.950 --> 00:06:57.240
So those are the state and federal laws

00:06:57.240 --> 00:07:00.380
that are most likely to apply
in this particular situation.

00:07:00.380 --> 00:07:03.240
So the question is, do
they actually apply?

00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:05.190
Did the president actually violate

00:07:05.190 --> 00:07:08.700
one of these criminal
election-related statutes?

00:07:08.700 --> 00:07:11.270
Well, as we've discussed
many times on this channel,

00:07:11.270 --> 00:07:14.900
often criminality requires
a specific mental state,

00:07:14.900 --> 00:07:17.900
a mens rea, and this case is no different.

00:07:17.900 --> 00:07:22.070
Sometimes the same actual
physical conduct can be criminal

00:07:22.070 --> 00:07:24.820
depending on the particular
mental state that someone had.

00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:26.260
And the criminal justice system

00:07:26.260 --> 00:07:28.880
is actually very, very concerned

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:31.310
with the intent that someone has.

00:07:31.310 --> 00:07:34.120
And here, most of the state
and federal election crimes

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:35.660
require mental states

00:07:35.660 --> 00:07:38.320
of either willfulness or intentionality.

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:40.950
And those carry very specific meanings

00:07:40.950 --> 00:07:43.030
in the world of criminal law.

00:07:43.030 --> 00:07:44.580
Willfulness is generally defined

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:46.280
as meaning the prosecutor must prove

00:07:46.280 --> 00:07:48.520
beyond a reasonable doubt
that the defendant knew

00:07:48.520 --> 00:07:51.090
that their conduct was
unlawful and intended

00:07:51.090 --> 00:07:53.280
to do something that the law forbids.

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:54.920
That is that they acted with a purpose

00:07:54.920 --> 00:07:57.450
to disobey or disregard the law.

00:07:57.450 --> 00:07:59.450
Now, many states define willfulness

00:07:59.450 --> 00:08:01.520
and intentionality slightly differently.

00:08:01.520 --> 00:08:05.250
It's a very ambiguous term
within the world of criminal law.

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:07.240
That's actually why people have tried

00:08:07.240 --> 00:08:09.840
to adopt what's called a model penal code,

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:11.430
but we'll save that for another day.

00:08:11.430 --> 00:08:13.640
Now, I looked and I
couldn't find how Georgia

00:08:13.640 --> 00:08:16.260
defines or construes its
willfulness requirement

00:08:16.260 --> 00:08:19.240
in the context of these
election law violations.

00:08:19.240 --> 00:08:20.073
But you will notice

00:08:20.073 --> 00:08:23.430
that the federal laws also use
the willfulness requirement.

00:08:23.430 --> 00:08:26.120
And there is some case law with respect

00:08:26.120 --> 00:08:27.550
to the federal laws here.

00:08:27.550 --> 00:08:29.070
For President Trump to be convicted

00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:31.230
under Section 242, for example,

00:08:31.230 --> 00:08:33.260
a prosecutor would have
to show three elements

00:08:33.260 --> 00:08:36.320
that he acted under color of
law, that he acted willfully,

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:38.460
and that he deprived or
attempted to deprive someone

00:08:38.460 --> 00:08:40.760
of the rights of the
constitution or federal law.

00:08:40.760 --> 00:08:43.160
And courts have interpreted Section 242

00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:45.940
to impose a specific intent requirement.

00:08:45.940 --> 00:08:48.440
The prosecutor would need to
show that the president acted

00:08:48.440 --> 00:08:51.230
with a specific intent to deprive someone

00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:54.410
of a constitutional right
or with an open defiance

00:08:54.410 --> 00:08:57.960
or in reckless disregard of
a constitutional requirement.

00:08:57.960 --> 00:08:59.670
And as always, the criminal justice system

00:08:59.670 --> 00:09:02.010
looks to the context and
circumstantial evidence

00:09:02.010 --> 00:09:03.350
to determine someone's mental state,

00:09:03.350 --> 00:09:05.280
because no one can read minds.

00:09:05.280 --> 00:09:07.560
And recall that circumstantial
evidence isn't weak,

00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:10.370
it's often the strongest
evidence that we have.

00:09:10.370 --> 00:09:12.290
So let's look to the call itself

00:09:12.290 --> 00:09:15.440
and see what a prosecutor and
a defense attorney would argue

00:09:15.440 --> 00:09:19.490
in the context of this call
and the general election.

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:21.550
Now, arguably President
Trump's greatest exposure

00:09:21.550 --> 00:09:24.270
is probably under the solicitation laws.

00:09:24.270 --> 00:09:27.210
President Trump seemingly
asked Brad Raffensperger

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:28.880
not to count legal votes.

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:30.710
He asked him to find the exact number

00:09:30.710 --> 00:09:32.890
of votes needed to overturn the result.

00:09:32.890 --> 00:09:35.880
Just one more than Joe
Biden got would do it.

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:37.130
In one portion of the call,

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:39.230
President Trump seemingly accuses

00:09:39.230 --> 00:09:41.920
both Brad Raffensperger
and the General Counsel

00:09:41.920 --> 00:09:44.110
for the Secretary of State, Ryan Germany,

00:09:44.110 --> 00:09:46.830
of engaging in criminal conduct.

00:09:46.830 --> 00:09:48.500
- [Donald] And you're
gonna find that they are,

00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:49.830
which is totally illegal.

00:09:49.830 --> 00:09:53.340
It's more illegal for
you than it is for them

00:09:53.340 --> 00:09:56.290
because you know what they did
and you're not reporting it.

00:09:58.732 --> 00:10:00.154
That's a criminal offense.

00:10:00.154 --> 00:10:02.440
And you can't let that happen.

00:10:02.440 --> 00:10:06.100
That's a big risk to you
and to Ryan, your lawyer.

00:10:06.100 --> 00:10:07.430
That's a big risk.

00:10:07.430 --> 00:10:09.705
- A threat that comes from the president

00:10:09.705 --> 00:10:10.538
of the United States

00:10:10.538 --> 00:10:12.720
who of course controls
the Department of Justice.

00:10:12.720 --> 00:10:15.960
He says that it's criminal
and you can't let that happen.

00:10:15.960 --> 00:10:16.793
It's a risk.

00:10:16.793 --> 00:10:20.330
It's a big risk to both
Raffensperger and Germany.

00:10:20.330 --> 00:10:22.060
When the president of the United States

00:10:22.060 --> 00:10:23.990
says that you're engaging
in criminal conduct,

00:10:23.990 --> 00:10:26.130
that carries a different kind of weight

00:10:26.130 --> 00:10:29.260
than when you're just
Joe Schmo on the street.

00:10:29.260 --> 00:10:31.790
And then right after
that particular section

00:10:31.790 --> 00:10:34.160
where he's saying that
the Georgia officials

00:10:34.160 --> 00:10:36.600
have engaged in criminal conduct,

00:10:36.600 --> 00:10:41.197
he then goes on to say that
he just wants 11,780 votes.

00:10:43.270 --> 00:10:44.103
- [Donald] You know, I mean,

00:10:44.103 --> 00:10:47.070
I'm notifying you that
you're letting it happen.

00:10:47.070 --> 00:10:49.970
So look, all I wanna do is this,

00:10:49.970 --> 00:10:54.970
I just wanna find 11,780 votes,

00:10:57.950 --> 00:11:00.520
which is one more than we have

00:11:00.520 --> 00:11:01.353
because we won the state.

00:11:01.353 --> 00:11:04.200
- And that number could
be incredibly important

00:11:04.200 --> 00:11:06.760
because he's not saying he wants all

00:11:06.760 --> 00:11:09.950
of the fraudulently cast
ballots or that he wants all

00:11:09.950 --> 00:11:14.310
of the incorrectly cast ballots
to be reversed in his favor.

00:11:14.310 --> 00:11:17.520
He wants specifically one more vote

00:11:17.520 --> 00:11:21.050
than Joe Biden won the state by.

00:11:21.050 --> 00:11:22.950
President Trump in many
different spots says

00:11:22.950 --> 00:11:27.910
that Joe Biden ostensibly
has won Georgia by 11,779.

00:11:27.910 --> 00:11:31.960
Thus President Trump wants
just one more than that.

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:33.680
And that could go a long way

00:11:33.680 --> 00:11:35.450
towards establishing the mens rea

00:11:35.450 --> 00:11:38.540
of the criminality that
he knows that the numbers

00:11:38.540 --> 00:11:42.540
are false and that he just
wants one single vote more.

00:11:42.540 --> 00:11:44.070
He doesn't care exactly how many he gets

00:11:44.070 --> 00:11:45.970
as long as he beats Joe Biden.

00:11:45.970 --> 00:11:48.980
And then arguably in
almost the next sentence,

00:11:48.980 --> 00:11:52.290
he says that he doesn't exactly
care how Georgia does it.

00:11:52.290 --> 00:11:54.660
Call it a mistake, call
it a recalculation,

00:11:54.660 --> 00:11:56.870
just do it and flip the state.

00:11:56.870 --> 00:12:00.710
- [Donald] And flipping the
state is a great testament

00:12:00.710 --> 00:12:05.710
to our country because it's a
testament that they can admit

00:12:06.490 --> 00:12:09.580
to a mistake or whatever
you wanna call it.

00:12:09.580 --> 00:12:11.110
If it was a mistake, I don't know.

00:12:11.110 --> 00:12:13.050
A lot of people think it wasn't a mistake,

00:12:13.050 --> 00:12:15.800
it was much more criminal than that.

00:12:15.800 --> 00:12:18.140
- And then President
Trump seemingly goes on

00:12:18.140 --> 00:12:20.140
to cajole the Georgia officials

00:12:20.140 --> 00:12:23.920
in speak that literally
sounds like a mobster.

00:12:23.920 --> 00:12:25.060
- [Donald] So what are
we gonna do here, folks?

00:12:25.060 --> 00:12:27.020
I only need 11,000 votes.

00:12:27.020 --> 00:12:30.263
Fellas, I need 11,000
votes. Give me a break.

00:12:31.295 --> 00:12:33.777
You know, we have that in spades already.

00:12:33.777 --> 00:12:36.560
- "What are we gonna do,
fellas? Give me a break.

00:12:36.560 --> 00:12:38.240
We have it in spades already."

00:12:38.240 --> 00:12:39.360
I mean, he really does seem

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:41.800
like he watched a bunch
of 1940s gangster movies.

00:12:41.800 --> 00:12:44.520
And President Trump just can't even fathom

00:12:44.520 --> 00:12:46.660
why a Republican official in Georgia

00:12:46.660 --> 00:12:48.590
wouldn't be trying to
do everything possible

00:12:48.590 --> 00:12:52.080
to give the election to
a Republican president.

00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:53.740
- [Donald] Why don't you
wanna find this, Ryan?

00:12:53.740 --> 00:12:54.950
What's wrong with you?

00:12:54.950 --> 00:12:57.700
I heard your lawyer is
very difficult actually,

00:12:57.700 --> 00:12:59.970
but I'm sure you're a good lawyer.

00:12:59.970 --> 00:13:02.170
You have a nice last name.

00:13:02.170 --> 00:13:04.370
But I'm just curious

00:13:07.198 --> 00:13:09.510
why do you keep fighting this thing?

00:13:09.510 --> 00:13:11.600
It just doesn't make sense.

00:13:11.600 --> 00:13:13.100
- And then President Trump goes on to say

00:13:13.100 --> 00:13:15.820
that they need to reexamine
the election results

00:13:15.820 --> 00:13:17.180
but they need to reexamine it

00:13:17.180 --> 00:13:19.590
with people that want to find the answers,

00:13:19.590 --> 00:13:21.910
seemingly implying that
they should use people

00:13:21.910 --> 00:13:26.910
who were in on the fix and
will actually flip the results.

00:13:27.260 --> 00:13:29.940
- [Donald] So tell me,
Brad, what are we gonna do?

00:13:29.940 --> 00:13:32.340
We won the election and it's not fair

00:13:32.340 --> 00:13:34.950
to take it away from us like this.

00:13:34.950 --> 00:13:38.790
And it's gonna be very
costly in many ways.

00:13:38.790 --> 00:13:43.080
And I think you have to say
that you're gonna reexamine it.

00:13:43.080 --> 00:13:44.470
And you can reexamine it,

00:13:44.470 --> 00:13:47.990
but reexamine it with people
that wanna find answers,

00:13:47.990 --> 00:13:50.170
not people that don't wanna find answers.

00:13:50.170 --> 00:13:53.540
- So assuming that the actual
acts here rise to the level

00:13:53.540 --> 00:13:55.230
of the various election crimes

00:13:55.230 --> 00:13:57.490
that we discussed and frankly,

00:13:57.490 --> 00:13:59.300
getting a Secretary of State

00:13:59.300 --> 00:14:01.600
to literally change the
votes to turn an outcome

00:14:01.600 --> 00:14:03.530
probably qualifies for a lot of the things

00:14:03.530 --> 00:14:05.790
that we previously talked about.

00:14:05.790 --> 00:14:08.780
A prosecutor would argue
that these statements show

00:14:08.780 --> 00:14:10.730
that President Trump does have

00:14:10.730 --> 00:14:13.470
the requisite mental
state for these crimes.

00:14:13.470 --> 00:14:16.460
And there is a specific
intent to violate the law

00:14:16.460 --> 00:14:18.270
and engage in criminality.

00:14:18.270 --> 00:14:20.130
A prosecutor would say President Trump

00:14:20.130 --> 00:14:22.140
is going after exactly the number of votes

00:14:22.140 --> 00:14:23.600
that's needed to flip the state,

00:14:23.600 --> 00:14:28.390
that he's recognizing that the information

00:14:28.390 --> 00:14:32.010
is against him and that he
doesn't seriously believe

00:14:32.010 --> 00:14:34.550
that he actually won the state,

00:14:34.550 --> 00:14:37.060
that he is threatening the officials

00:14:37.060 --> 00:14:39.990
in charge of the election
results in Georgia.

00:14:39.990 --> 00:14:42.340
Not only that, but later on in the tapes,

00:14:42.340 --> 00:14:46.460
he talks about how all the
good things will happen

00:14:46.460 --> 00:14:49.030
to Raffensperger and Germany

00:14:49.030 --> 00:14:50.910
if they do flip the state in his favor.

00:14:50.910 --> 00:14:52.310
So he's offering both carrots

00:14:52.310 --> 00:14:54.780
and sticks to change the results.

00:14:54.780 --> 00:14:57.520
And it appears that he's
single-mindedly focused

00:14:57.520 --> 00:15:00.240
on the outcome rather than the process.

00:15:00.240 --> 00:15:01.610
On the other hand, a defense attorney

00:15:01.610 --> 00:15:04.700
for President Trump would
argue based on the context

00:15:04.700 --> 00:15:08.370
of the call and on the explicit
language of the call itself

00:15:08.370 --> 00:15:11.120
that President Trump did
not engage in criminality.

00:15:11.120 --> 00:15:13.560
That the statements that
we just talked about

00:15:13.560 --> 00:15:15.350
make sense in context.

00:15:15.350 --> 00:15:17.070
And certainly everyone would agree

00:15:17.070 --> 00:15:19.050
that President Trump never explicitly said

00:15:19.050 --> 00:15:23.010
invent fake votes so that
he wins the election.

00:15:23.010 --> 00:15:24.380
It appears that throughout the call,

00:15:24.380 --> 00:15:26.990
President Trump has an honest belief,

00:15:26.990 --> 00:15:28.540
a subjective honest belief that may

00:15:28.540 --> 00:15:31.070
or may not comport with objective reality,

00:15:31.070 --> 00:15:33.040
but nonetheless an honest belief

00:15:33.040 --> 00:15:35.080
that there was fraud in Georgia.

00:15:35.080 --> 00:15:37.300
- [Donald] The bottom
line is many, many times,

00:15:37.300 --> 00:15:42.300
the 11,779 margin that
they said we lost by,

00:15:43.980 --> 00:15:48.980
we had vast, I mean, the
state is in turmoil over this,

00:15:50.830 --> 00:15:53.480
and I know you would like
to get to the bottom of it.

00:15:53.480 --> 00:15:54.590
- He seems fixated by it.

00:15:54.590 --> 00:15:59.590
He seems to believe everything
that the social media

00:15:59.820 --> 00:16:01.870
or as he calls it, the Trump media.

00:16:01.870 --> 00:16:04.730
He says he does not watch social media,

00:16:04.730 --> 00:16:06.500
he watches Trump media,

00:16:06.500 --> 00:16:09.640
but he appears to believe everything

00:16:09.640 --> 00:16:12.690
that those sources are saying.

00:16:12.690 --> 00:16:15.693
- [Donald] And also that
Dominion took out machines.

00:16:16.580 --> 00:16:18.910
That Dominion is really moving fast

00:16:18.910 --> 00:16:22.820
to get rid of their machinery.

00:16:22.820 --> 00:16:24.653
Do you know anything about that?

00:16:26.180 --> 00:16:27.080
Because that's illegal.

00:16:27.080 --> 00:16:28.170
- [Ryan] This is Ryan Germany.

00:16:28.170 --> 00:16:31.250
No, Dominion has not moved any machinery

00:16:31.250 --> 00:16:32.083
out of Fulton County.

00:16:32.083 --> 00:16:33.750
We're having an election on Tuesday.

00:16:35.113 --> 00:16:37.150
- [Donald] Have they moved the inner parts

00:16:37.150 --> 00:16:40.443
of the machines and replaced
them with other parts?

00:16:42.000 --> 00:16:43.501
- [Ryan] No.

00:16:43.501 --> 00:16:45.350
- [Donald] Are you sure, Ryan?

00:16:45.350 --> 00:16:47.520
- [Ryan] I'm sure, I'm
sure, Mr. President.

00:16:47.520 --> 00:16:51.830
- It's total nonsense, but he
seems to actually believe it.

00:16:51.830 --> 00:16:56.830
So in the context of that,
of the Trump news media,

00:16:57.250 --> 00:16:58.500
and President Trump is looking

00:16:58.500 --> 00:17:01.050
into ways of addressing the fraud

00:17:01.050 --> 00:17:03.240
that he honestly believes took place.

00:17:03.240 --> 00:17:06.700
And yes, President Trump
referred to the number 11,780

00:17:06.700 --> 00:17:08.880
which is a very convenient
number for the president.

00:17:08.880 --> 00:17:10.680
That's a number that would flip Georgia.

00:17:10.680 --> 00:17:12.840
But really, throughout the call,

00:17:12.840 --> 00:17:14.450
President Trump is referring to lots

00:17:14.450 --> 00:17:18.370
of different numbers related
to the claimed election fraud.

00:17:18.370 --> 00:17:22.540
At some times talking about
300,000 mysterious ballots

00:17:22.540 --> 00:17:26.817
or quote, massive numbers
far greater than the 11,779.

00:17:28.700 --> 00:17:31.300
Or he says that accurate numbers

00:17:31.300 --> 00:17:34.370
would include more than
fifties of thousands.

00:17:34.370 --> 00:17:37.520
He's convinced that there are far more

00:17:37.520 --> 00:17:40.600
than the number of votes
necessary for him to win,

00:17:40.600 --> 00:17:43.710
and he's just concerned
about finding enough.

00:17:43.710 --> 00:17:45.470
At one point he says he doesn't want to go

00:17:45.470 --> 00:17:47.070
after Dominion because he doesn't need to,

00:17:47.070 --> 00:17:50.260
because there are all these other votes

00:17:50.260 --> 00:17:54.630
that were fraudulently cast
that total far more than 12,000.

00:17:54.630 --> 00:17:56.310
So therefore they don't even need

00:17:56.310 --> 00:17:58.440
to get into the Dominion thing.

00:17:58.440 --> 00:18:00.530
And at the same time,
the president's lawyer,

00:18:00.530 --> 00:18:02.190
Cleta Mitchell of Foley &amp; Lardner

00:18:02.190 --> 00:18:03.830
says that what they're trying to get

00:18:03.830 --> 00:18:05.650
is the data from Georgia,

00:18:05.650 --> 00:18:09.640
that Georgia for legal
and privacy reasons,

00:18:09.640 --> 00:18:11.370
has not disclosed a lot

00:18:11.370 --> 00:18:13.140
of the election-related data to them,

00:18:13.140 --> 00:18:15.040
so they actually can't check some

00:18:15.040 --> 00:18:17.070
of these fraud-related
claims and they simply

00:18:17.070 --> 00:18:19.900
want the data to be
able to make that check,

00:18:19.900 --> 00:18:23.140
though that may seemingly
be illegal in and of itself.

00:18:23.140 --> 00:18:24.850
- [Cleta] I think what president's saying

00:18:24.850 --> 00:18:27.490
and what we've been trying
to do is to say, look,

00:18:27.490 --> 00:18:30.080
the court is not acting on our petition.

00:18:30.080 --> 00:18:32.020
They haven't even assigned a judge,

00:18:32.020 --> 00:18:33.710
but the people of Georgia and the people

00:18:33.710 --> 00:18:37.070
of America have a right
to know the answers

00:18:37.070 --> 00:18:41.230
and you have data and records
that we don't have access to.

00:18:41.230 --> 00:18:43.740
- And then unfortunately
there's the additional problem

00:18:43.740 --> 00:18:45.440
that a lot of the president's thoughts

00:18:45.440 --> 00:18:47.030
are completely inchoate.

00:18:47.030 --> 00:18:49.390
The problem is the
president has brain worms.

00:18:49.390 --> 00:18:50.253
- Brain worms.

00:18:51.290 --> 00:18:54.060
- At one point in the call, he
says that he literally thinks

00:18:54.060 --> 00:18:56.930
that he won every state in the country.

00:18:56.930 --> 00:18:58.490
- [Donald] Oh, every single state.

00:18:58.490 --> 00:18:59.460
We won every state,

00:18:59.460 --> 00:19:02.020
we won every State House in the country.

00:19:02.020 --> 00:19:06.300
- So when someone's head is
filled with complete nonsense,

00:19:06.300 --> 00:19:08.770
that actually has a big effect in terms

00:19:08.770 --> 00:19:12.960
of trying to prove a subjective,
specific intent crime.

00:19:12.960 --> 00:19:15.660
So a prosecutor would
say that you have to read

00:19:15.660 --> 00:19:19.010
between the lines, you have to
read the subtext to the text

00:19:19.010 --> 00:19:21.520
and that just like no mafia don

00:19:21.520 --> 00:19:25.140
would ever say explicitly
commit the crime itself.

00:19:25.140 --> 00:19:27.500
It's meant through implication.

00:19:27.500 --> 00:19:29.700
And that you have to look at the leverage

00:19:29.700 --> 00:19:31.620
and the pressure that someone is putting

00:19:31.620 --> 00:19:33.320
on another person to commit a crime.

00:19:33.320 --> 00:19:35.310
While a defense attorney would say

00:19:35.310 --> 00:19:38.490
this is just someone that
is extremely concerned

00:19:38.490 --> 00:19:41.390
about the election who
has honest, if crazy,

00:19:41.390 --> 00:19:43.400
beliefs about that election

00:19:43.400 --> 00:19:45.890
and that they're just trying
to explore the legal avenues

00:19:45.890 --> 00:19:50.890
to come to the outcome that
they believe is the right one.

00:19:51.250 --> 00:19:53.260
And then finally there is the question

00:19:53.260 --> 00:19:56.450
of apart from the potential
criminality itself,

00:19:56.450 --> 00:19:58.690
could this behavior be impeachable,

00:19:58.690 --> 00:20:01.890
just the implication
of the context itself?

00:20:01.890 --> 00:20:04.650
And the answer to that
is almost certainly yes.

00:20:04.650 --> 00:20:07.870
Congress has wide discretion to impeach

00:20:07.870 --> 00:20:11.330
and the Senate to remove
based on impropriety.

00:20:11.330 --> 00:20:13.210
And it's hard to believe that even

00:20:13.210 --> 00:20:17.860
if the phone call itself was not criminal,

00:20:17.860 --> 00:20:20.480
that based on the context

00:20:20.480 --> 00:20:23.180
and the implications that the president

00:20:23.180 --> 00:20:24.780
either knew or should have known

00:20:24.780 --> 00:20:28.060
that what he was doing was
improper in the context

00:20:28.060 --> 00:20:32.870
of a democratic republic and
thus it's removable conduct.

00:20:32.870 --> 00:20:36.300
But it appears that President
Trump finally got his wish.

00:20:36.300 --> 00:20:40.380
He finally found the election
fraud that he was looking for.

00:20:40.380 --> 00:20:42.730
And when Susan Collins
said that she thought

00:20:42.730 --> 00:20:45.030
that President Trump
had learned his lesson

00:20:45.030 --> 00:20:48.670
from the last perfect phone
call and the last impeachment,

00:20:48.670 --> 00:20:51.510
it appears that he did learn a lesson

00:20:51.510 --> 00:20:54.350
that he should just do it again.

00:20:54.350 --> 00:20:55.440
But on the other hand,

00:20:55.440 --> 00:20:57.190
it appears that the Democratic member

00:20:57.190 --> 00:20:58.930
of the Georgia State Election Board

00:20:58.930 --> 00:21:01.290
has formally asked the
Georgia Secretary of State

00:21:01.290 --> 00:21:04.520
to open an investigation into
possible criminal violations

00:21:04.520 --> 00:21:07.200
by President Trump
based on the phone call.

00:21:07.200 --> 00:21:09.660
So it's anyone's guess as
to what's going to happen

00:21:09.660 --> 00:21:12.030
to President Trump as a
result of this phone call,

00:21:12.030 --> 00:21:15.723
both while he's in office and
eventually when he leaves.

